{
  "_comment": "SEDRA (#13): Miningcore (branch sedra-merged-mining) for the public testnet: Kaspa testnet-10 as the parent, the Sedra testnet as the merged-mined chain. A separate instance with its own database; never the production pool's host, database or wallets. UPPERCASE values are placeholders. genesisHash MUST be the Sedra testnet genesis: without it Miningcore commits to the mainnet genesis and every Sedra block is rejected (WrongCommitment). ZKas (D11, 2026-11-25): a private ZKas test chain is merged next to Sedra; its genesisHash MUST be the ZKas testnet genesis (Miningcore defaults to ZKas mainnet), and its pool address MUST be a shielded zkastest:p... address (ZKas testnet rejects a coinbase paying a transparent address); zkas-walletd runs on the pool host (127.0.0.1:8501) and walletPassword is its X-Wallet-Token. rewardCrossCheckUrl 'off': Miningcore otherwise cross-checks rewards against the mainnet explorers, and the synthesized Sedra aux pool does not inherit it, so that pool is written out as its own entry. Coinbase budget: Kaspa allows 204 payload bytes; ZKM1 (68) + SDM1 (47) + Miningcore's '2.1.0.' prefix leave about 24 bytes for extra.extraData, so keep it short. Miners give a ZKas test address in the user name (kaspatest:...+zkastest:...); a zkastest: address in the password is ignored by Miningcore today. Hosts as installed 2026-11-25: the pool on VM 204, the Kaspa testnet-10 node and the ZKas test node on VM 206 (192.168.0.28).",
